# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Gambaran Keseluruhan {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the Constrained Quantum Optimizer by Aqarios, you can solve constrained binary optimization problems on IBM&reg; quantum hardware without manual reformulation and circuit mapping. Simply supply a problem as an LP file, an MPS file, or a [Luna Model](https://docs.aqarios.com/luna-model). The function handles reformulation, circuit synthesis, transpilation, and hardware execution automatically. The solver utilizes iterative warm-starting [\\[1\\]](#references) of the [FlexQAOA](https://docs.aqarios.com/luna-solve/algorithms/quantum-gate/flexqaoa/) algorithm, a constraint-native extension of the Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA).\n"
msgstr "Dengan Constrained Quantum Optimizer oleh Aqarios, anda boleh menyelesaikan masalah pengoptimuman binari terkekang pada perkakasan kuantum IBM&reg; tanpa perlu memformulasi semula secara manual dan pemetaan litar. Cukup bekalkan masalah sebagai fail LP, fail MPS, atau [Model Luna](https://docs.aqarios.com/luna-model). Fungsi ini mengendalikan pemformulaan semula, sintesis litar, transpilasi, dan pelaksanaan perkakasan secara automatik. Penyelesai ini menggunakan warm-starting berulang [\\[1\\]](#references) bagi algoritma [FlexQAOA](https://docs.aqarios.com/luna-solve/algorithms/quantum-gate/flexqaoa/), iaitu lanjutan constraint-native bagi Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The optimizer targets binary problems with constraints. In particular, one-hot constraints and set-packing constraints can be natively enforced by using XY-mixers. Other constraint types are automatically reformulated as penalty terms.\n"
msgstr "Pengoptimum ini menyasarkan masalah binari dengan kekangan. Khususnya, kekangan one-hot dan kekangan set-packing boleh dikuatkuasakan secara semula jadi dengan menggunakan XY-mixers. Jenis kekangan lain diformulasi semula secara automatik sebagai terma penalti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Description {#description}"
msgstr "Penerangan {#description}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Disclaimer\">\n"
"Performance can depend on both the problem instance and subsequent processing steps. In some cases, classical samples and quantum-generated samples might achieve similar final solution quality after equivalent post-processing. Evaluation should therefore consider the complete optimization workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Penafian\">\n"
"Prestasi boleh bergantung kepada kedua-dua instans masalah dan langkah pemprosesan seterusnya. Dalam sesetengah kes, sampel klasik dan sampel yang dijana secara kuantum mungkin mencapai kualiti penyelesaian akhir yang serupa selepas pasca-pemprosesan yang setara. Oleh itu, penilaian harus mempertimbangkan keseluruhan aliran kerja pengoptimuman.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Constrained Quantum Optimizer implements the Iterative warm-start XY-mixer QAOA(IWS-QAOA) [\\[1\\]](#references). The algorithm runs fixed-angle QAOA circuits on quantum hardware and updates the initial warm-start probabilities of each circuit using measurement outcomes from the previous iteration. No variational parameter training is required; instead, a fixed linear ramp parametrization is chosen.\n"
msgstr "Constrained Quantum Optimizer melaksanakan Iterative warm-start XY-mixer QAOA (IWS-QAOA) [\\[1\\]](#references). Algoritma ini menjalankan litar QAOA sudut-tetap pada perkakasan kuantum dan mengemas kini kebarangkalian warm-start awal bagi setiap litar menggunakan hasil pengukuran daripada lelaran sebelumnya. Latihan parameter variasi tidak diperlukan; sebaliknya, parametrisasi ramp linear tetap dipilih.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By using XY-mixers to enforce one-hot constraints, you can drastically improve solution quality for constrained problems, because the search space is practically reduced to a smaller feasible subspace &mdash; and no additional complexity, due to penalty terms, is introduced in the optimization landscape.\n"
msgstr "Dengan menggunakan XY-mixers untuk menguatkuasakan kekangan one-hot, anda boleh meningkatkan kualiti penyelesaian dengan ketara untuk masalah terkekang, kerana ruang carian secara praktikalnya dikurangkan kepada subruang boleh laksana yang lebih kecil &mdash; dan tiada kerumitan tambahan, akibat terma penalti, diperkenalkan dalam landskap pengoptimuman.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Workflow {#workflow}"
msgstr "Aliran Kerja {#workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow of the function is described below:\n"
msgstr "Aliran kerja fungsi ini diterangkan di bawah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Preprocessing**: Before circuit synthesis, the optimizer analyzes the constraint structure of the input problem:\n"
msgstr "**Prapemprosesan**: Sebelum sintesis litar, pengoptimum menganalisis struktur kekangan masalah input:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Graph preprocessing:_ When applicable to the problem, it is analyzed as a graph, where edges determine the relationship between variables. This graph analysis enables two preprocessing problem enhancements. First, single constraints can be aggregated to one large constraint by using clique merging, so that they are represented by a single XY-mixer. Second, variables with only a single neighbor can be fixed deterministically, reducing the problem size and complexity.\n"
msgstr "_Prapemprosesan graf:_ Apabila berkenaan dengan masalah, ia dianalisis sebagai graf, di mana tepi menentukan hubungan antara pemboleh ubah. Analisis graf ini membolehkan dua penambahbaikan prapemprosesan masalah. Pertama, kekangan tunggal boleh digabungkan menjadi satu kekangan besar dengan menggunakan penggabungan klik (clique merging), supaya ia diwakili oleh satu XY-mixer sahaja. Kedua, pemboleh ubah yang hanya mempunyai satu jiran boleh ditetapkan secara deterministik, mengurangkan saiz dan kerumitan masalah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Constraint resolution:_ The preprocessor handles each constraint separately: If the constraint is a one-hot constraint, it can be enforced through XY-mixers. If it is a set-packing constraint, it will first be transformed to a one-hot constraint. Equality constraints are handled through quadratic penalties, and inequality constraints through [unbalanced penalization](https://doi.org/10.1088/2058-9565/ad35e4).\n"
msgstr "_Penyelesaian kekangan:_ Praprosesor mengendalikan setiap kekangan secara berasingan: Jika kekangan itu adalah kekangan one-hot, ia boleh dikuatkuasakan melalui XY-mixers. Jika ia adalah kekangan set-packing, ia akan diubah terlebih dahulu kepada kekangan one-hot. Kekangan kesamaan dikendalikan melalui penalti kuadratik, dan kekangan ketaksamaan melalui [unbalanced penalization](https://doi.org/10.1088/2058-9565/ad35e4).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Penalty derivation:_ Constraints that cannot be expressed as one-hot equality constraints are converted to penalty terms. The optimizer derives the penalty strength automatically from the problem structure.\n"
msgstr "_Terbitan penalti:_ Kekangan yang tidak dapat dinyatakan sebagai kekangan kesamaan one-hot ditukar kepada terma penalti. Pengoptimum menerbitkan kekuatan penalti secara automatik daripada struktur masalah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Iterative warm-starting**: The optimizer runs multiple _parallel warm-start chains_. Each chain holds a probability distribution over variable assignments, which is used as the starting probability of the QAOA circuit (warm-start state). At each iteration, a chain samples from the quantum circuit, applies classical postprocessing, and updates its distribution based on the occurrence of samples. Across iterations, this focuses the search on high-quality solutions without a variational optimization loop.\n"
msgstr "**Warm-starting berulang**: Pengoptimum menjalankan pelbagai _rantai warm-start selari_. Setiap rantai memegang taburan kebarangkalian ke atas penetapan pemboleh ubah, yang digunakan sebagai kebarangkalian permulaan litar QAOA (keadaan warm-start). Pada setiap lelaran, satu rantai mengambil sampel daripada litar kuantum, menerapkan pasca-pemprosesan klasik, dan mengemas kini taburannya berdasarkan kejadian sampel. Merentasi lelaran, ini memfokuskan carian kepada penyelesaian berkualiti tinggi tanpa gelung pengoptimuman variasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of chains (`num_parallel`), the total shot budget per chain (`total_shots`), and the number of QAOA repetitions (`reps`) are the primary controls for trading solution quality against runtime.\n"
msgstr "Bilangan rantai (`num_parallel`), jumlah bajet tangkapan (shot) setiap rantai (`total_shots`), dan bilangan pengulangan QAOA (`reps`) merupakan kawalan utama untuk mengimbangi kualiti penyelesaian dengan masa jalan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Workflow diagram of the Constrained Quantum Optimizer](/docs/images/guides/aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer/cqo-diagram.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Workflow diagram of the Constrained Quantum Optimizer](/docs/images/guides/aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer/cqo-diagram.svg)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarks {#benchmarks}"
msgstr "Penanda Aras {#benchmarks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The benchmarks below show that the Constrained Quantum Optimizer Qiskit Function is capable of finding high quality, feasible solutions to constrained optimization problems with well above 100 binary variables. Accuracy is the ratio of the found objective value to the known optimum. Runtime is wall-clock time from function invocation to result delivery. QPU usage is the billable Quantum Compute time.\n"
msgstr "Penanda aras di bawah menunjukkan bahawa Fungsi Qiskit Constrained Quantum Optimizer mampu mencari penyelesaian berkualiti tinggi dan boleh laksana untuk masalah pengoptimuman terkekang dengan lebih daripada 100 pemboleh ubah binari. Ketepatan (accuracy) ialah nisbah nilai objektif yang ditemui kepada optimum yang diketahui. Masa jalan (runtime) ialah masa jam-dinding daripada panggilan fungsi hingga penyampaian hasil. Penggunaan QPU ialah masa Pengkomputeran Kuantum yang boleh dicaj.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two problems were examined: The [Maximum Independent Set](/tutorials/find-the-maximum-independent-set-with-aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer) (MIS) problem and the Max-$k$-Cut, which is an extension of the well-known MaxCut problem to more than two categories. Max-$k$-Cut is also the optimization problem equivalent of the graph coloring decision problem (when all edges are cut, the graph is $k$-colorable).\n"
msgstr "Dua masalah dikaji: masalah [Maximum Independent Set](/tutorials/find-the-maximum-independent-set-with-aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer) (MIS) dan Max-$k$-Cut, iaitu lanjutan bagi masalah MaxCut yang terkenal kepada lebih daripada dua kategori. Max-$k$-Cut juga merupakan masalah pengoptimuman yang setara dengan masalah keputusan pewarnaan graf (graph coloring) (apabila semua tepi dipotong, graf itu boleh diwarna-$k$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem               | Variables | Constraints | Qubits | Accuracy | Feasibility | Total runtime (s) | QPU usage (s) | Total shots |\n"
"|-----------------------|-----------|-------------|--------|----------|-------------|-------------------|---------------|-------------|\n"
"| MIS es60fst02         | 186       | 280         | 124    | 100.0%   | True        | 940.2             | 147.0         | 25.0k       |\n"
"| MIS sloane\\_2dc\\_128  | 128       | 5173        | 74     | 100.0%   | True        | 347.6             | 106.0         | 12.5k       |\n"
"| Max-3-Cut Karate Club | 99        | 33          | 99     | 98.7%    | True        | 279.5             | 166.0         | 25.0k       |\n"
"| Max-4-Cut Karate Club | 132       | 33          | 132    | 100.0%   | True        | 258.3             | 200.0         | 25.0k       |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Masalah               | Pemboleh ubah | Kekangan | Qubit | Ketepatan | Kebolehlaksanaan | Jumlah masa jalan (s) | Penggunaan QPU (s) | Jumlah tangkapan |\n"
"|-----------------------|-----------|-------------|--------|----------|-------------|-------------------|---------------|-------------|\n"
"| MIS es60fst02         | 186       | 280         | 124    | 100.0%   | True        | 940.2             | 147.0         | 25.0k       |\n"
